Package: wsiTools
Title: Tools for Reading, Tiling, Converting and Exporting Whole-Slide Images
Version: 0.1.13
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Stefano", family = "Caccia",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "tkcaccia@gmail.com")
Author: Stefano Caccia [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Stefano Caccia <tkcaccia@gmail.com>
Description: A lightweight R toolkit for memory-efficient whole-slide image
    access and preprocessing through region-based reading, tiling, pyramidal
    image handling, conversion and export. The core uses light R dependencies
    plus a small native bridge for optional accelerated routines. OpenSlide,
    libvips, ZEISS libCZI, StarDist, Cellpose, OME-Zarr pixel access, and
    web-service integrations are optional runtime capabilities discovered
    through explicit backend checks. The package avoids loading complete
    whole-slide images into R memory by default.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
